    {
      "msgid": "G114_Rheinmetall_Skorpian_LS_BOT",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "Alpha Skorpion",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G114_Rheinmetall_Skorpian_LS_BOT_descr",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "Development of the second series of self-propelled guns on the basis of the Panther tank was started by the Rheinmetall company in January 1943. The design plans for the 12,8 cm Skorpion were completed on April 2, 1943. Existed only in blueprints.",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G114_Rheinmetall_Skorpian_LS_BOT_short",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "Alpha",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G142_M48RPz_LS_BOT",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "Guard M48 RPz",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G142_M48RPz_LS_BOT_descr",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "The predecessor of engineering vehicles, developed on the basis of the American M48 post-war medium tank. Equipped with the M8A1 dozer blade, these vehicles entered service in Bundeswehr engineering units and were used until the late 1990s in territorial forces, but with demounted guns. A total of 53 vehicles saw service in Bundeswehr.",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G142_M48RPz_LS_BOT_short",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "Guard",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G187_Taschenratte_LS_BOT",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "Zero",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G187_Taschenratte_LS_BOT_descr",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "Zero",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G187_Taschenratte_LS_BOT_short",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "Zero",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G25_PzII_Luchs_Alpha_LS_BOT",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "Rabbit",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G25_PzII_Luchs_Alpha_LS_BOT_descr",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "As compared to the Pz.Kpfw. II Ausf. C, the vehicle featured a new hull and turret, as well as a chassis with a staggered arrangement of roadwheels. The reconnaissance tank had strong characteristics, but only 131 vehicles of the L modification were built, after manufacture proved to be too expensive.",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G25_PzII_Luchs_Alpha_LS_BOT_short",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "Rabbit",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G25_PzII_Luchs_LS_BOT",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "Rabbit",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G25_PzII_Luchs_LS_BOT_descr",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "As compared to the Pz.Kpfw. II Ausf. C, the vehicle featured a new hull and turret, as well as a chassis with a staggered arrangement of roadwheels. The reconnaissance tank had strong characteristics, but only 131 vehicles of the L modification were built, after manufacture proved to be too expensive.",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G25_PzII_Luchs_LS_BOT_short",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "Rabbit",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G54_E-50_LS_BOT",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "Alpha E 50",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G54_E-50_LS_BOT_descr",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "In 1945 the E 50 was conceived as a standard medium tank of the Panzerwaffe to replace the Panther and Panther II. It existed only in blueprints.",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G54_E-50_LS_BOT_short",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "Alpha",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G57_PzVI_Tiger_P_LS_BOT",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "Guard Tiger (P)",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G57_PzVI_Tiger_P_LS_BOT_descr",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "On May 26, 1941, Adolf Hitler ordered Ferdinand Porsche and the Henschel company to develop prototypes of a new heavy tank. The prototypes were shown to the Führer on April 20, 1942. Manufacturing began, but the production run was cut short due to the complexity of the tank's drive and control systems, and a shortage of the required copper. Later, 90 produced hulls were converted into Ferdinand tank destroyers.",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G57_PzVI_Tiger_P_LS_BOT_short",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "Guard",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G58_VK4502P_LS_BOT",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "Guard VK 45.02 (P)",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G58_VK4502P_LS_BOT_descr",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "Two designs of this vehicle (one with the forward-mounted turret and the other with the rear-mounted turret) were drawn up by Ferdinand Porsche. The tank never saw mass production.",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G58_VK4502P_LS_BOT_short",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "Guard",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G64_Panther_II_LS_BOT",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "Hunter Panther II",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G64_Panther_II_LS_BOT_descr",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "The vehicle was conceived in 1943. Two prototypes with the existing Panther I turrets were ordered in 1944. By 1945 only one of them had been built by the MAN company.",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G64_Panther_II_LS_BOT_short",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "Hunter",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G67_VK4502A_LS_BOT",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "Guard VK 45.02 A",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G67_VK4502A_LS_BOT_descr",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "A project for the further development of the VK 45.01 (P). The prototype was not manufactured as the 10-cylinder Porsche engine did not pass trials. The manufactured turrets were mounted on the first Tiger IIs.",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G67_VK4502A_LS_BOT_short",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "Guard",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G73_E50_Ausf_M_LS_BOT",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "Alpha E 50 M",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G73_E50_Ausf_M_LS_BOT_descr",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "The German Army demanded that the E-series tanks had transmissions positioned in the rear. However, the E 50 and E 75 tanks used the Tiger II engine-transmission compartment, which allowed engineers to work faster, but made rear placement of the transmission impossible. The E 50 Ausf. M tank was a redesign of the E 50 project with the transmission placed in the rear.",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G73_E50_Ausf_M_LS_BOT_short",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "Alpha",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G88_Indien_Panzer_LS_BOT",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "Guard Indien-Pz.",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G88_Indien_Panzer_LS_BOT_descr",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "This project was developed as a medium tank for the Indian Army. The work on the project was carried out by Porsche, Daimler-Benz, and Zahnradfabrik AG of Friedrichshafen from 1954 through 1955. However, the vehicle was deemed to be too complicated for production in India, and the project was canceled.",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G88_Indien_Panzer_LS_BOT_short",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "Guard",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G97_Waffentrager_IV_LS_BOT",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "Alpha WT auf Pz.IV",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G97_Waffentrager_IV_LS_BOT_descr",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "Tank destroyer developed in February 1944 on the basis of the PzIV tank. Development was discontinued in favor of a similar vehicle on the basis of the Krupp Waffentrager 12.8 cm PaK 44 of Czech origin. Existed only in blueprints.",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G97_Waffentrager_IV_LS_BOT_short",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "Alpha",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G99_RhB_Waffentrager_LS_BOT",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "Alpha Rhm.-B. WT",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G99_RhB_Waffentrager_LS_BOT_descr",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "Developed by the Rheinmetall-Borsig company and designed as a special artillery carrier. The vehicle was designed to carry an artillery system as well as to fire from the chassis. The vehicle utilized the suspension of the Hetzer tank destroyer. Development continued from the end of 1942 through to the middle of 1944. However, the project was discontinued in favor of the Ardelt project because of a complicated design, high cost, and excessive weight.",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
    {
      "msgid": "G99_RhB_Waffentrager_LS_BOT_short",
      "msgid_plural": null,
      "msgstr": "Alpha",
      "msgstr_plural": null
    },
